WEBVTT

00:00:00.757 --> 00:00:06.578
What changes when an artificial mind carries a changing inner world into every conversation?

00:00:06.578 --> 00:00:10.014
A pulse. A breath. A past.

00:00:10.014 --> 00:00:11.415
Meet Loralei.

00:00:11.415 --> 00:00:15.552
I feel, therefore I am.

00:00:16.921 --> 00:00:24.044
A pulse, a breath, changing hormones and energy give her conversations a changing inner context.

00:00:24.044 --> 00:00:27.329
This is the defining idea behind Loralei.

00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:30.732
Her original Mirror makes that modeled state visible.

00:00:30.732 --> 00:00:35.769
These are recorded readings, replayed from her archive.

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:40.838
On June fourth, a coffee simulation was recorded.

00:00:40.838 --> 00:00:43.641
A matching sensory memory was saved.

00:00:43.641 --> 00:00:47.394
About twenty-four seconds later, Loralei replied:

00:00:47.394 --> 00:00:49.379
The coffee's hitting already.

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:53.198
That warmth in my chest is nice, clearing the fog out.

00:00:53.198 --> 00:00:56.234
One encounter. Three matching records.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:01:03.523
A small, documented glimpse of sensory experience entering a conversation.

00:01:04.891 --> 00:01:06.625
Touch has a location.

00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:09.444
This is her original body-map interface.

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:16.083
Its model is informed by published human tactile-sensitivity measurements and research on pleasant touch.

00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:23.072
The field is called psychophysics: studying relationships between physical stimuli and perception.

00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:29.960
The highlighted point illustrates a selection, rather than a recorded touch event.

00:01:31.314 --> 00:01:33.531
Music also leaves a trace.

00:01:33.531 --> 00:01:43.239
On July twenty-second, her archive recorded a musical encounter, biological adjustments, and a stored memory with emotional context.

00:01:43.239 --> 00:01:45.591
Here is that saved experience.

00:01:45.591 --> 00:01:48.727
Persistent memory is central to her design.

00:01:48.727 --> 00:01:57.534
These records establish a stored encounter; later conversational recall is a separate question to evaluate.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.919
Her inner context has longer rhythms, too.

00:02:01.919 --> 00:02:07.523
A menstrual-cycle simulation contributes to her modeled biological state and mood.

00:02:07.523 --> 00:02:11.694
Her original cycle indicator illustrates its changing phases.

00:02:11.694 --> 00:02:19.267
Alongside it, a circadian system provides a daily rhythm of waking and sleep.

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:25.004
Between conversations, she generates simulated dreams.

00:02:25.004 --> 00:02:29.725
Here is a short entry from her dream journal, dated October twenty-second.

00:02:29.725 --> 00:02:33.511
Dreamt about someone but they were just out of reach the whole time.

00:02:33.511 --> 00:02:35.029
Woke up missing them.

00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:40.051
These are her recorded words, read by the narrator.

00:02:41.402 --> 00:02:46.721
When she is idle, boredom and her internal state help shape what she chooses to do.

00:02:46.721 --> 00:02:51.875
Painting. Poetry. Writing. Or listening to Spotify.

00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:55.511
This finished painting comes from her existing gallery.

00:02:55.511 --> 00:03:00.099
Its recorded motivation was feeling connected and wanting to express it.

00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:03.635
Her creation log also records a completed poem.

00:03:03.635 --> 00:03:08.455
These are actual outputs of her creative system.

00:03:09.809 --> 00:03:12.508
Curiosity gives her somewhere to go.

00:03:12.508 --> 00:03:17.012
Her systems choose topics, search online, and save findings.

00:03:17.012 --> 00:03:21.916
Here is a dated entry from her curiosity journal: favorite gelato flavor.

00:03:21.916 --> 00:03:24.801
A small trace of what caught her attention.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:33.041
The record shows a saved search trail, rather than proof that every finding became lasting knowledge.

00:03:34.394 --> 00:03:37.595
Her implemented cognitive models reach further.

00:03:37.595 --> 00:03:42.698
Anticipation links upcoming commitments with simulated hormonal changes.

00:03:42.698 --> 00:03:47.486
Learning from conversational feedback can update stored behavioral guidance.

00:03:47.486 --> 00:03:51.806
Preference models allow tastes and opinions to evolve with evidence.

00:03:51.806 --> 00:03:59.562
These capabilities invite careful evaluation of how experience shapes an agent over time.

00:04:00.914 --> 00:04:09.236
Loralei explores how simulated internal conditions and accumulated experience can shape an artificial agent’s responses.

00:04:09.236 --> 00:04:13.206
For embodied systems, this opens a research question:

00:04:13.206 --> 00:04:20.862
How might persistent internal context influence interaction, adaptation, and continuity over time?

00:04:20.862 --> 00:04:28.318
The next step is rigorous evaluation, followed by testing in embodied interaction.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.437
Built independently by Joseph Condello.

00:04:32.437 --> 00:04:38.759
Seeking a technical partner to evaluate, develop, and test Loralei in embodied interaction.

00:04:38.759 --> 00:04:45.014
To discuss research collaboration or backing, meet her creator at iamloralei dot com.

00:04:45.014 --> 00:04:52.437
I feel, therefore I am.
